00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.220
This scene is the climax in
the first half of the show.

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:54.260
If this is how it's going to be,
we're better off not doing it.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.530
Please wait!

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:59.660
I'll try harder! Please give me
one more chance!

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:01.700
Miss Layla!

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:06.940
I figured as much.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.240
Or rather, she has way too little talent.

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:12.010
It's like, I might be the only one
who can do it.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.320
I wonder if they're going to cancel the show.

00:05:14.320 --> 00:05:16.010
If that keeps up, they just might.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.350
Mia!

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:29.260
Are you all right?

00:05:29.260 --> 00:05:31.790
You've been doing this every morning
without breaks.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:32.940
I'm all right.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:35.700
Idiot! If you keep this up, you'll get hurt.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.530
But I have to. Because I can't do it.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:42.100
Why don't you quit then?

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.380
It's so third-rate to give up
for a reason like that.

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:46.820
Such a loser.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:48.150
It's her again!

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.420
You know her?

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:52.720
Marion, don't interrupt their practice!
Marion!

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:54.090
Okay!

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.500
Who's that?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:01.400
No idea.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:02.700
No idea?

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:06.340
That's Marion. She's the daughter of
Jean, the sceneman.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.460
So that's who she is.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.830
Still, she went too far with what she said.

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:14.100
Her mother used to be a star trampoliner.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:16.740
She also loves the trampoline.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.980
She's also talented and people used to
have high expectations of her.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:23.120
But after her mother died,
she quit trampoline.

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:24.380
Her mother?

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:27.290
Yeah. She collapsed suddenly
and died soon after.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:30.920
After that, Marion became
sarcastic like that.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:32.890
I see...

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.000
But still, she said too much.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:35.990
I guess.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.900
Oh, Mia.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.100
I'm okay. Please leave me alone.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.130
Mia...

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:48.740
Mia's grandma is hospitalized
and her surgery date is

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:51.110
the same day as the
opening day for Cinderella.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:55.220
Surgery? So Mia can't show her
real abilities because

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:57.090
she's worried about her
grandma's surgery.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:59.920
Not really. It's more like
she's trying too hard.

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:01.120
What?

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:06.030
Her grandma is the one most looking
forward to seeing Mia on stage.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.600
I heard that when Mia learned
she had been cast,

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:11.600
she sent her grandma an e-mail saying
that she would do her best,

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:13.040
so her grandma should do the same too.

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:16.300
I see. That's why she was pushing
herself so hard.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.400
But Mia has the tendency to lose her cool
when she tries too hard.

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:24.300
Sorry, Grandma.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:29.320
I may not be able to keep my promise.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.160
Make the fairy godmother role
a part for three people?

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:36.290
What do you think?

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:37.280
Three?

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.660
Oh, I think it sounds great!

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.130
Wouldn't that make it even more difficult?

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:44.700
But I'd feel more reassured
if Anna and Sora are with me.

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:45.430
What?

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:45.800
What?

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:45.800
What?

00:07:45.800 --> 00:07:46.390
What?

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:47.900
That means...

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:48.930
In short...

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.400
The cast members would be...

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.800
So the cast members are
Anna, Sora, and myself!

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:57.810
WHAT?! Me?!

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.910
Yeah. You don't want to?

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:01.020
No. I'm not saying that, but...

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:02.220
I'm okay with it,

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:04.910
but I'm not sure if we can get him
to change the cast now.

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:06.380
Fine, then.

00:08:07.820 --> 00:08:09.020
It's an interesting idea.

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:11.880
I will tell the director about it.

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.630
Make sure to come up with something
Layla will be satisfied with.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:20.000
Then you mean you don't mind me
getting on stage?

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:22.130
I'll decide that after I see the results.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:25.300
But the time limit is three days.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.980
If you're not ready in three days,

00:08:27.980 --> 00:08:32.110
I will cancel Cinderella as Layla
suggested. Got it?

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.750
Yes, sir! We will do our best!

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:52.200
I can't believe Boss said okay.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:55.140
Since we've gotten this far,
we have to be ready for the show.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:56.500
I'm grateful to both of you.

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.940
No, I'm the one who should be grateful.

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:02.980
Sora?

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.100
What's the matter?

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.210
I have fun handing out toys to kids
in the audience now,

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:11.520
but I still want to appear on stage.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:14.490
And now, thanks to Mia,
my wish may come true.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:17.290
Let the three of us join forces and

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.330
appear on stage together!

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:20.320
Yeah.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:25.700
After that, this is the climax and

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:30.570
all of us jump towards
the center like this. Oh...

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:40.150
I wonder if handing off wands while
doing a cross jump

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:41.650
is impossible after all?

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:43.780
Yeah. It could be.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:46.860
Mia, why don't we change it into
something more simple?

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:51.090
We can't, because we have to convince
both Boss and Miss Layla.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.860
I wish I could find a better idea.

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:57.090
When you think of Cinderella...

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.370
Glass slippers! When you
think of Cinderella...

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.000
A pumpkin prince!

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:03.810
There's no such thing.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:05.410
Oh, really?

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:06.340
That's it.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:08.310
That's it!

00:10:08.310 --> 00:10:09.780
What do you mean?

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:11.580
A pumpkin prince?!

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.420
All right! I'll take that role!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:14.250
No, that's not it.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:15.250
No way!

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:17.950
Wait, let me try the idea
on the simulator.

00:10:19.190 --> 00:10:21.290
We'll install some kind
of device in the wands.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:25.920
When we cross jump, we spread out
a big cloth like magic.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:29.460
And then, make it look like a big
pumpkin like this.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:30.520
What do you think?

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:32.030
Ooh...

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.240
I see. A pumpkin.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.010
Which means if we don't fall at the
right moment together from the top,

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:40.270
it won't become the shape of a pumpkin.

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:43.550
I know. And once we successfully
make the pumpkin,

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:45.740
Cinderella will appear from inside.

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:48.150
Amazing! It's like magic.

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:51.610
If we can make the audience think that,
it'll really be magic.

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:54.250
A spell cast by the three of us.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:56.020
Oh, it needs a name.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:58.230
How about something like "Triple Illusion"?

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.100
Triple Illusion?

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:02.060
Yeah, this maneuver's name.

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:03.400
It sounds good.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:06.860
All right, intensive training for the
Triple Illusion begins tomorrow!

00:11:07.300 --> 00:11:08.370
Let's do our best!

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:09.360
Yes!

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:19.570
I have to work hard.
For Mia's sake and for myself.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.780
This is a long awaited chance.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.720
Why are you so flustered?

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.850
Any normal person would be!

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.530
I need to tell you something. Lay down here.

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:31.730
No, thank you.

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:33.760
Then I will talk to you like this.

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:34.850
Like this?

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:38.690
I will get right to the point. You should not
pair up with those two girls.

00:11:39.130 --> 00:11:40.190
What?

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:42.100
The skill levels are far too disparate.

00:11:44.170 --> 00:11:46.110
I already know that.

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:49.100
It's true that I suck, but this is my chance.

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:51.940
No, I did not mean it like that. Oh.

00:11:54.320 --> 00:11:56.610
Please make sure to turn off the light.
Good night.

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:03.080
The reverse Star. A failure.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.090
Hurry up and turn off the light.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:06.350
Right.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.010
Sorry...

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.480
It's my fault.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:32.680
Don't keep blaming just yourself.

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.990
I just couldn't catch it.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.320
I hate it!

00:12:42.700 --> 00:12:44.820
I just keep making mistakes.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:56.270
I'm sorry.

00:12:56.650 --> 00:13:00.010
We failed because our moves
didn't match up.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:02.580
So, it wasn't just your fault.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:04.610
Right, Mia?

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:07.410
Mia...

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:10.930
If you think I shouldn't be part of it,
please feel free to say so.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:11.390
I didn't say that.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:11.390
If you think I shouldn't be part of it,
please feel free to say so.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.490
I didn't say that.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:14.730
No, you didn't.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.630
My timing was also a little off,
so it could be my fault.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:19.530
It's my idea's fault.

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:21.560
My idea was just impossible to begin with.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:25.640
As I thought, you're third-rate!

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:30.370
I don't want people like you
up on the trampoline!

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:34.650
Moping around about whose fault it was.
You guys are losers!

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:37.620
What's the matter with you?
This has nothing to do with you.

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:40.690
It does too!

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:45.220
Because... Because... the trampoline was...

00:13:45.830 --> 00:13:49.490
my mom's... my mom's favorite...

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:55.230
Marion...

00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:57.430
Marion!

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:00.730
Sorry about the weird things Marion said.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:04.400
Please let me know whenever you need
a trampoline adjustment.

00:14:08.650 --> 00:14:10.620
Come on, let's practice, practice.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:14.150
Miss Layla...

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:16.690
Um...

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:19.060
I think having three people play
the fairy godmother

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:21.050
will be a selling point for the upcoming show.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:23.400
Thank you.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:27.170
That is why we need to make sure it is
perfect before the show starts.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.900
Yes, we will do our best.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.410
Sora and Anna, please step down
from this role.

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:32.430
What?

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:36.810
Perfect this routine using you,
Charlotte, and Julie.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.980
But the Triple Illusion is supposed to
be done by Sora, Anna, and myself.

00:14:39.980 --> 00:14:41.680
We are not doing this for fun.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:44.390
And I'm only inviting you to be a part of it

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:46.150
because I heard this was your idea.

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:50.150
If you don't like it, I will ask you
to step down as well.

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:55.300
Mia...

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:55.560
Anna, let's go.

00:14:55.300 --> 00:14:55.560
Mia...

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:56.530
Anna, let's go.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:57.730
But...

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.830
Never mind. Please excuse us.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:03.000
I guess it's just the difference in talent,
you know?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.670
It's like, sorry for being so talented.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:22.710
Here you go.

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:26.360
Oh, thank you very much.

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.350
Sorry about that.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:31.160
You're upset about what Marion said,
aren't you?

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.430
Oh, no. I'm okay about that.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:34.870
But...

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:39.030
Well, it's kind of a long story, but...

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:41.570
So that's what happened.

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:44.280
And the three of you were working
so hard at it, too.

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:48.150
Oh, don't worry about it. It's my fault.

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:50.190
By the way, where's Marion?

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:53.660
Oh, she's probably hiding somewhere
here in the lesson hall.

00:15:53.660 --> 00:15:55.560
She's always like that when she's sulking.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.590
Oh well, she'll be back once she gets hungry.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:15:59.890
Excuse me...

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:00.760
What is it?

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.730
About what Marion said earlier...

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:03.700
Oh...

00:16:03.700 --> 00:16:06.940
Does it have something to do with
the way Marion behaves?

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:09.300
That is, if you don't mind.
Would you tell me about it?

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.300
Have you already heard that
her mother passed away?

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:16.370
Six years ago,

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:20.700
my wife, Cynthia, was a star
at Kaleido Stage.

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:26.320
She was an earnest woman
who loved to practice.

00:16:26.990 --> 00:16:29.390
There is no such thing as wasted practice.

00:16:29.390 --> 00:16:32.550
We can be confident because
we practice every day.

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:36.390
Without that confidence, our performance
wouldn't make anyone happy.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:41.960
But because she seldom took a break,
she might have made Marion lonely.

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:45.070
Then one day, Marion had a fever.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:50.240
It was unusual for her, but Marion asked
Cynthia not to go on stage that day.

00:16:51.250 --> 00:16:53.920
But since there was no one who could
substitute for Cynthia,

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:55.610
she went on stage.

00:16:56.220 --> 00:17:00.850
However, on that particular day,
Cynthia made a big mistake.

00:17:02.090 --> 00:17:02.590
Mom, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
It's because I was being so spoiled.

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:06.360
She was taken to the hospital right away,
but her condition wasn't good.

00:17:02.590 --> 00:17:06.360
Mom, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
It's because I was being so spoiled.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:07.000
Mom, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.
It's because I was being so spoiled.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:12.520
It's not your fault, Marion. It was my
mistake, so it's no one's fault.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:16.040
Besides, Mom's going to recover from
these injuries really soon,

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:20.000
and I'll show you even more
amazing performances.

00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:22.880
Those were Cynthia's last words

00:17:22.880 --> 00:17:26.140
and she passed away without ever
setting foot on stage again.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.580
Ever since, in Marion's opinion,

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:31.350
no trampoliner better than
Cynthia has appeared.

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:34.320
She can't be satisfied with
anyone's performance

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:36.150
and she became sarcastic like that.

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:41.650
So that's what happened.
Marion must've really loved her mom.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:45.690
And she must also love the Kaleido Stage
that her mom loved so much.

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:47.760
Thank you.

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:50.300
I'd like to thank you too.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.230
I'm glad that I had a chance
to hear your story.

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:56.110
When you think about it, it's weird for me
to get depressed about it.

00:17:56.310 --> 00:18:00.380
Mia's the one who gave me the possibility
of appearing on stage.

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:03.250
Yet, I made Mia feel bad.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.090
If I'd been able to do everything properly,

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:08.180
Mia wouldn't have had to be so torn.

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:11.850
I'll practice much harder.

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:48.920
Good morning, Marion.

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:50.590
Dad...

00:18:51.030 --> 00:18:53.130
She's been practicing before
the crack of dawn.

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:56.730
Your mom used to do the same before
a new show opened, remember?

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:58.190
Yeah.

00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:17.890
Mom!

00:19:19.730 --> 00:19:21.560
Ouch!

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:25.200
Oh? Anna, good morning.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:27.170
Don't "Good morning" me.

00:19:27.170 --> 00:19:29.190
You're still the same reckless risk-taker.

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:32.110
Sorry.

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:32.610
This is no time to be laughing.

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:32.610
Sorry.

00:19:32.610 --> 00:19:33.970
This is no time to be laughing.

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.310
I'll practice with you.

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:39.250
Mia...

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:42.540
Where are Charlotte and Julie?
You're not practicing with them?

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:44.590
I stepped down from the role.

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:45.620
What?

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:47.920
But you already told your grandma...

00:19:47.920 --> 00:19:51.690
I thought about it and I'd rather
perfect it with you two.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:55.460
I'm sure my grandma would also agree
that's the better thing to do.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:56.450
Mia...

00:19:56.830 --> 00:19:57.900
I'm sorry.

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.840
I should have said so right away yesterday.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.370
Are you really sure about giving up on this?

00:20:03.370 --> 00:20:06.070
No, I haven't given up yet.

00:20:06.070 --> 00:20:06.840
What?

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:12.540
I asked them, "Please give us a chance
to show you our Triple Illusion.

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:15.450
If it's still not good enough,
we'll resign from our roles."

00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:16.810
I see.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:18.210
Mia...

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:22.090
I believe they will become first-rate
Kaleido Stars.

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:23.730
Me too.

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:25.430
Then, let's practice right away.

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:26.360
Okay.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:28.660
I'll try slowing down my spin a little,

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.670
so, Sora, can you try to speed up yours?

00:20:30.670 --> 00:20:31.770
Okay, I'll do that.

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:34.940
Then, I'll throw in my orangutan pose
in the middle.

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:35.870
Please don't!

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:38.440
We have one day left. Let's work hard.

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:39.530
Yeah!

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:42.010
Just now, Mom...

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.910
No, it's nothing.

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:47.620
Dad, I'm hungry.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:49.240
Okay, let's have breakfast.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:55.820
The upright Star. Hope.

00:20:57.260 --> 00:20:59.620
She changed the future.

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:09.430
Come on, you three,
it's almost time to start.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:10.640
Okay!

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:57.740
What do you think?

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:00.210
You can hardly call this first-rate.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.360
But it looked like you were also
on the edge of your seat.

00:22:04.130 --> 00:22:07.420
Those girls certainly are
strangely captivating.

00:22:08.800 --> 00:22:11.160
Kalos, you take the responsibility
to perfect it.

00:22:12.330 --> 00:22:14.130
I guess it means that they passed.

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:16.200
The Triple Illusion.

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:24.410
<i>When you sabishii toki doushitemasuka</i>

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:24.410
<i>When you're lonely, what do you do?</i>

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:26.850
<i>Never say sonna no wakannai</i>

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:26.850
<i>Never say you don't get any of that</i>

00:22:26.850 --> 00:22:29.750
<i>Nemuru asobu magazine mekuru</i>

00:22:26.850 --> 00:22:29.750
<i>Sleep, play, flip through a magazine</i>

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:32.050
<i>Sabishii toki wa sabishii yo</i>

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:32.050
<i>When you're lonely, you're lonely</i>

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:36.860
<i>Mienai denpa ga kyou mo
tulututu machi ni tobikau</i>

00:22:32.050 --> 00:22:36.860
<i>Like always, invisible vibes fly around
the city today, tulututu</i>

00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:41.500
<i>Anyway kokoro no bekutoru
so many reason hanashiteru</i>

00:22:36.860 --> 00:22:41.500
<i>Anyway, the vector of my heart is
talking about so many reasons</i>

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:46.200
<i>Jiyuu ni sora o tobitai keredo</i>

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:46.200
<i>I want to be free and fly the skies</i>

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:50.870
<i>Hane o hirogeru basho ga nai</i>

00:22:46.200 --> 00:22:50.870
<i>But I don't have space to spread my wings</i>

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:53.070
<i>Demo shinjiteru</i>

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:53.070
<i>But I have faith</i>

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:57.710
<i>Katachi no nai mirai ga aru yo</i>

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:57.710
<i>There is a future yet to be shaped</i>

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:02.420
<i>Katachi ni shitai watashi ga iru</i>

00:22:57.710 --> 00:23:02.420
<i>And there's a me that I want to shape</i>

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:08.890
<i>Kanashikutemo machigai demo</i>

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:08.890
<i>Even if I'm sad, even if it's a mistake</i>

00:23:08.890 --> 00:23:14.230
<i>Omou mama fly to the free</i>

00:23:08.890 --> 00:23:14.230
<i>I'll do what I want and
fly towards the freedom</i>

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:21.770
Next Kaleido Star

00:23:21.770 --> 00:23:22.070
Sora, let's go home together.

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:23.300
Sora, let's go home together.

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:26.040
I'm not leaving for Japan until you say
that you're coming with me.

00:23:26.040 --> 00:23:28.140
And so, on the opening day for Cinderella,

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:30.180
my dad suddenly came to
America from Japan.

00:23:30.180 --> 00:23:31.950
He says he's going to take
Sora back with him.

00:23:31.950 --> 00:23:34.750
I understand how your dad feels,
but let's do our best together!

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:36.050
Everyone, I'm sorry.

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:37.020
WHAT?!

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:38.790
My feelings for my family and my dream.

00:23:38.790 --> 00:23:41.780
What should I do, I wonder?
I wonder? I wonder?

00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:42.960
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"My Amazingly Distant Family"

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:45.390
My Amazingly Distant Family

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:45.390
Next time on Kaleido Star,
"My Amazingly Distant Family"

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:47.790
My Amazingly Distant Family

00:23:45.390 --> 00:23:47.790
My wings are my dream
and on towards the sky...
